In article <20473@hacgate.UUCP> hayes%bh_ddemo3@valkris.hac.com writes:
|You enter an opulent throne room containing Medusa (no, that green @ is
|*not* a woodland elf!).  You have the following items at your 
|disposal:
|1.  Excalibur +3.
|2.  A mirror.
|4.  Wand of Cancellation
|5.  Wand of Make invisible.
|6.  Wand of lighting (0 or less charges)
|7.  Amulet of life saving.
|8.  Complete set of armour (except boots) from the elven armoury.
|9.  Pick-axe
|10. a lamp (1)
|11. a mirror
|12. a bugle.
|Your intrinsics include: teleportation (no control), and telepathy.
|Known spells: charm monster, sleep, slow monster.

1) Assuming the Wand of lightning has 0 charges, step out of the room and
Engave with it until you are blinded.  Then walk 1 square away from Medusa
and (a)pply one of the mirrors towards her twice.

2) Zap the wand of Make invisible at Medusa-that way you cannot see her.  
But be warned: wand invisibility can leave at any moment, so be sure to chop
her up with Excalibur immediately.

3) Put Medusa to sleep (via spell), walk one square away from her, and 
(a)pply the mirror twice.

4) Close all the doors to the throne room and pray that there's only one
Medusa on the level, and she cannot open doors.  Come back when you have a
blindfold or a potion of blindness.

